    // Moved here from right after showAdmin()'s own definition, near the top
    // of this script -- showAdmin() calls into functions/reads consts (e.g.
    // TL_PAGE/tlList, declared much further down for the Page Layout section)
    // that don't exist yet that early in the file's top-level evaluation
    // order. Calling it immediately on a page load where a session already
    // exists hit that TDZ and threw -- which, since it's a synchronous
    // top-level throw, silently aborted the rest of this script's own
    // evaluation, including every event listener below the throw point
    // (logout button included). Running this only after every other
    // top-level declaration in the file has finished evaluating avoids it
    // entirely, without having to hunt down or reorder every individual
    // thing showAdmin() touches.
    if (sessionStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY)) {
      showAdmin();
